net: usb: r8152: fix transmit queue timeout

Upstream commit 833dcd75d54f0bf5aa0a0781ff57456b421fbb40
("net: usb: r8152: fix transmit queue timeout") by Mingj Ye,
Reviewed-by: Hayes Wang <hayeswang@realtek.com>.

Problem
=======
When the TX queue length reaches the threshold, rtl8152_start_xmit() calls
netif_stop_queue().  Transmissions do not stop though: write_bulk_callback()
-> tx_bottom() keeps calling r8152_tx_agg_fill() and submitting bulk-out URBs
while there are queued skbs and free aggregations.

Because ndo_start_xmit is no longer invoked while the queue is stopped,
txq->trans_start stops being refreshed.  After watchdog_timeo (5s) the netdev
watchdog treats an actively transmitting device as stalled and fires:

    NETDEV WATCHDOG: eth1 (r8152): transmit queue 0 timed out
    WARNING: CPU: ... at net/sched/sch_generic.c dev_watchdog

That false alarm is destructive, because rtl8152_tx_timeout() unconditionally
calls usb_queue_reset_device(), i.e. a USB port reset:

    static void rtl8152_tx_timeout(struct net_device *netdev, unsigned int txqueue)
    {
            netif_warn(tp, tx_err, netdev, "Tx timeout\n");
            usb_queue_reset_device(tp->intf);
    }

Some RTL8153B units do not survive that reset.  They stop answering
SET_ADDRESS and drop off the bus:

    r8152-cfgselector 4-1: Device not responding to setup address.
    r8152-cfgselector 4-1: device not accepting address 2, error -71
    usb usb4-port1: Cannot enable. Maybe the USB cable is bad?
    usb usb4-port1: attempt power cycle

On boards without a switchable VBUS regulator (NanoPi R2S: every regulator is
regulator-always-on and the dwc3 node has no vbus-supply) the hub's power cycle
request is a no-op, so the NIC stays dead until the board is physically
unplugged -- and a soft reboot does not help either, because VBUS never drops.

Fix
===
Refresh the transmit timestamp on every successful asynchronous URB submission
in r8152_tx_agg_fill(), so the watchdog tracks actual transmission activity and
only fires on a genuine stall.

Backported to linux-5.15 (immortalwrt 23.05, 5.15.198) for
friendlyarm_nanopi-r2s.  Verified against the pristine 5.15.198
drivers/net/usb/r8152.c; does not collide with
hack-5.15/760-net-usb-r8152-add-LED-configuration-from-OF.patch, which only
touches the init functions.

--- a/drivers/net/usb/r8152.c
+++ b/drivers/net/usb/r8152.c
@@ -2339,6 +2339,8 @@ static int r8152_tx_agg_fill(struct r8152 *tp, struct tx_agg *agg)
 	ret = usb_submit_urb(agg->urb, GFP_ATOMIC);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		usb_autopm_put_interface_async(tp->intf);
+	else
+		netif_trans_update(tp->netdev);
 
 out_tx_fill:
 	return ret;
